steam-arm-setup (2.3) stable; urgency=low

  * x86 client on Armv8.0 CPUs without LSE atomics: Valve's x86 client
    through system FEX in place of stop (steam-for-linux #13288);
    warning, memory check (2 GB), forwarding route only; native client
    check per setup run moves back once native build runs; --client=,
    --client-check, Maintenance > Client type; CLIENT keys not restored
    from backups. STEAM_ARM_ALLOW_ARMV80=1 keeps native client.
  * Settings menu Components: Parts and Driver archive (download, local
    copy of published archive, custom archive); steam-arm-config
    driver-archive command; status row Driver archive.
  * Published driver archive beside installer used when SHA-256 matches;
    local archive path saved (PROVIDER_LOCAL_FILE); saved file gone or
    changed: download with note; --provider-default clears it.
  * --detect prints driver archive line.
  * Driver archive recipe: verify step library check runs again.
  * Profile key diskcache=on|off: FEX code cache per title (FEX tool
    2609.1 or newer); cache deleted once after FEX tool or game build
    change.
  * Maintenance, Caches and steam-arm-config cache: FEX code cache
    sizes, clear all or one game; Steam shader cache never deleted.
  * 32-bit Source engine titles: Windows build (Proton ARM64,
    proton_11-arm64) set automatically on mali-csf-v10 (FEX tool up to
    2609, vk-spoof chosen), once per title; settings menu Graphics,
    Automatic Windows build; steam-arm-config auto-build; AUTO_BUILD key.
    Record decides for titles Steam swapped to Windows files; shared
    content manifests (LastOwner 0) skipped, also in settings menu game
    lists; Graphics screen text matches notice.
  * x86 client: file check at first start (marker x86-verified); private
    host libX11 copy with non-fatal X error handler; switch back to
    native client drops package records, native client checks its files
    at next start; stale launch wrapper copy removed; client home records
    its client type, so setup for another account checks only folders
    x86 client used.
  * --client-check: Armv8.1 CPU runs any build; result recorded as
    CLIENT_PROBE.
  * Renderer check: no CPU verdict for FEX loader process; Wine helper
    processes never named as title.
  * x86 client stop waits 45 s before SIGTERM; native client end by
    signal logged.
  * GE-Proton: interrupted download reported with curl status; lock
    file removed after each action; log path on own line in failed
    screen.
  * Settings menu: rows wrap with indent, dialog --no-collapse, whiptail
    list height per entry count, wizard Back keeps hardware choice,
    download gauge percent; cache sizes unknown without read access;
    dialog and whiptail text boxes use terminal height.
  * Setup restarts running tray (setup lock and output not inherited,
    summary names restart); local driver archive line for file named in
    environment, also with Mali tree already built.
  * x86 client: setup fetches runtime package runtime_scout_ubuntu12;
    launcher names missing runtime; first sign-in in desktop window;
    x86 program check accepts file 5.4x output (Intel i386).
  * Setup for another account drops records of previous account
    (kwinrules-made names account, owned.sha lines).
  * Settings menu Games header: Steam Deck category (hint).
  * CPU drawing notice (off by default): settings menu Graphics,
    steam-arm-config cpu-notice, CPU_NOTICE key; game lists mark
    titles drawn on CPU with CPU!.
  * --detect: vulkan features native / missing lines (vk-spoof set);
    Information row Vulkan gaps.
  * Tray icon with dark outline for light panels.
  * Removal deletes kwinrulesrc that setup created once it is empty.
  * Optional GE-Proton ARM64 install: settings menu Maintenance,
    GE-Proton (ARM64); steam-arm-config ge-proton; sha512 check,
    unpacked as game account; per-game pick (compat <appid> ge);
    removal per version and on uninstall; off until installed.
  * Launcher: one client start at once; start during first start
    shows progress notice and exits, client untouched; tray Open items
    greyed meanwhile.
  * Icon redraw at first start: KDE icon change signal after drawing;
    drawn once client icon file keeps its size.
  * Tray Steam pages (Store, Library, Friends, Downloads, Screenshots,
    Steam Settings) pass steam:// link to running client through
    steam-arm --open; tray item Steam ARM Settings.
  * Host package libibus-1.0-5 (steamwebhelper of native client loads
    it; Raspberry Pi OS desktop lacks it). Launcher warning names
    library steamwebhelper cannot load and its package; hardware report
    shows such lines.

