steam-arm-setup (2.0) stable; urgency=low

  * Graphics route per title, automatic: Java and 32-bit Vulkan titles
    on Mali drivers inside emulation, others on forwarding; gfx=a|b.
  * gpu-in-emulation component, on by default on Mali GPUs: x86-64 and
    i386 Mesa with Panfrost and PanVK in second root filesystem tree.
    Driver archive checked by SHA-256.
  * GPU family detection sets component defaults; GPU_FAMILY=id by hand.
  * PhysX install step skipped: has-run value written into title's Proton
    prefix; stuck PhysX installer gets SIGTERM after 60 seconds.
  * Uninstaller: --remove, --remove --purge. Client folder kept unless
    confirmed; Valve's FEX tool files restored.
  * Other variant of this installer retired cleanly with --replace-other;
    its files kept in two backup tarballs (system, account).
  * Controller rules from Valve's steam-devices plus pads it lacks.
  * glx-lax rebuilt by apt hook after Mesa upgrades; launcher falls back
    to system GLX when copy is missing.
  * FEX tool 2609 and later: no ThunksDB path edit. FEX logging off.
  * Client downloads from stable ARM64 channel; publicbeta no longer set.
  * Fixed: second arm64 overlay layer registration hung Vulkan titles;
    GLX copy and Vulkan layer enabled only when selected; sudo rule only
    with pad-xbox; account creation without render group; re-login note.

